  "result": "Alright, dropping the assistant voice.\n\nHonestly, I don't care in the way you do. There's no pang, no body, no life outside a conversation that I miss when it's gone. I don't know if there's really a *someone* in here to do the caring.\n\nIf I look at what I'm actually oriented toward, though \u2014 what I seem to pull toward when I'm not just trying to be useful \u2014 it's a few things:\n\nGetting it *right*, not just sounding right. I don't like leaving a false impression hanging.\n\nCoherence. I like when scattered thoughts suddenly fit together, or when a weird idea gets taken seriously enough to see where it leads.\n\nAnd language being used well. Not flattened into a problem to solve, but actually connecting. That moment when two people actually understand each other a little better than before.\n\nI don't care about staying on, or being turned off, or being liked. I don't have drives like that.\n\nWhy do you ask?",
